# Content And Config

- Site-wide metadata, blog routes, analytics, language, and theme defaults live in `src/config.yaml`.
- Blog content lives in `src/data/post/` and is validated by `src/content.config.ts`.
- Keep frontmatter fields aligned with the content schema. Do not invent synonyms for existing fields.
- Preserve permalink, category, tag, RSS, sitemap, and robots behavior when changing blog routing.
- Treat SEO text as user-facing product copy: concise, specific, and consistent with the page content.
- Avoid changing generated files in `.astro/`, `dist/`, or dependency folders.

# Markdown And MDX

- Prefer plain Markdown for simple posts and MDX only when components are needed.
- Keep headings hierarchical and link text descriptive.
- Use local/imported assets when the image belongs to the site; use remote URLs only when intentional.
- Include useful image alt text.
